// A trait declares `static` and then writes a default body that uses `self`. The trait breaks its
// own promise, so it is the same E0015 an implementor would get — the contract is checked against
// the body that stands in for every implementation exactly as it is against each real one.
//
// Without this the modifier would be trustworthy only where somebody wrote an `impl`: a trait whose
// static default reads `self` and that nobody implements yet would still license `T.m(…)` in a
// generic body, and the first implementor to omit the method would inherit a body with no receiver.
// expect: error E0015 at 12:15
// expect: exit 1
trait Codec {
    fn width(): int
    static fn tag(): string { return "codec ${self.width()}" }
}
echo "unreached"
